 "about": "What pickups and hazards do to a character, tried on one lane. The player starts at x = -15 and is held on D from second 3 to 15: a coin at x = -11 gives the status boots (speed +40 % for six seconds: the track should show about 7 m/s instead of 5.2), one at x = -3 gives snare (rooted for two seconds: the track stands still, then goes on), a big coin at x = 4 is a bumper (launcher, direction away, 10 m/s: the walk is thrown back). At 16 the player is put at x = 6 and walks into an unseen wall at x = 10 (a prefab of the empty model with extra collision): it should stop near x = 9.7. At level second 26 the stage graph knocks the player down; with revive set to two seconds, by itself, without the screen, the track should jump back to the respawn point at x = -15. Expect HZ_GO, HZ_BOOTS, HZ_SNARE, HZ_DOWN, and read playerTrack.",
